A||||7||Jason Kamrud||Make it a whole new car!!||||1||
Z||000000||Jason Kamrud||07-05-2001||09:36 PM||||Has anyone out there besides me fallen in love with the dashes & instruments on the newer Grand Am's & Grand Prix & even the Firebirds? I was looking at their interiors in like the '99 & newer Pontiacs & I really like that look. Even the Firebird dashes look pretty good. There are all kinds of these cars on the road, and getting to be more wrecked ones in the junkyards.<P>So I was thinking...if these things are being scrapped out, wouldn't it be cool to try & put the dash(minus the air bags) out of one of these into a Fiero! It would be close for width, and at least the gauges wouldn't be orange!  Of course it would almost take an electrical engineer to rig up the instruments & stuff...unless...hey, just swap in the 3.4 & computer & everything! That would be the thing to do.<P>Has anyone out there done this, or done anything even close to this? That would be the ultimate...to find a newer, low miles grand prix that some kid has rolled & totaled for like 3 grand. Swap in a stock 3.4 with all the bells & whistles, it would be a direct bold-in. Just swap in the wiring harness(hopefully it wouldn't have to be extended) and you'd have a whole new car!<P>This idea has been pounding on my head for quite a while now. If there is anyone out there who has done this, or anyone out there crazy enough to try doing this, please let me know because I am VERY curious! This would be the best complete upgrade, and you'd even be able to use all Poncho parts!<P>------------------<BR>Jason Kamrud||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||07-05-2001||10:10 PM||||Anythings possible I imagine. Ive always liked the Fiero's interior though...always thought it was a really cool setup. M7F||||reg||1
Z||000002||Devotshka||07-05-2001||10:35 PM||||I saw a picture somewhere where a person had installed a late-90s Bonneville dash into a fiero.  Not sure how much work something like that would be, but i see enough of that dash in my Bonneville, don't need to see it in my fiero too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Also, a guy that used to live near me had put an early-90s buick digital-speedo equipped dash... Regal i think it was, into his 84 coupe.  He said it was pretty straightforward apart from a few wiring issues.<BR>I guess anything is possible if you are motivated enough.... any of those 2000 pontiac dashes would spruce up the interior to suit my tastes just fine.||||reg||3
